[Music]  what dimension are you even in  [Music]  my dad was old enough and lucky enough  to have watched the original series when  it aired and I grew up watching the  reruns with my dad it was always a  special time and they would do these  marathon Twilight zones here in Los  Angeles  on TV and we would sit there and we'd  watch all day long every episode and you  know he had his own personal memories of  him and I created my own personal  memories and always loved them and they  were really seminal for me in terms of  inspiring the kind of work that I wanted  to do genre work and trying to work with  this different theme sort of woven into  it but it's not just the story and how I  got involved what this one was I started  talking to CBS about doing a reimagining  or a reboot of the original series and  then I had a general meeting with Jordan  Peele and Jordan I just started talking  about different things that we loved and  different things there were sort of  inspirations for us growing up and  Twilight Zone was kind of number 1 or 2  on the list for both of us and then we  started talking about what would happen  if we did it together  he was obviously somebody whose work I  admire greatly and it was kind of  perfect he suited to doing that modern  Twilight Zone but he was kind of  intimidated by it at first the same  where I was because it's such a big  mental yeah and then and then we just  started the more we talked about it the  more we felt like we could honor the  original series but do something  ourselves original and unique and update  it and make it feel like a really  genuine and contemporary version of  Twilight Zone that's a question I had  going into it too because I was like  it's a reboot it's a reimagining  are you guys going to remake any classic  episodes or is it more just like about  paying homage and moving forward it's  both every now and then we'll do like a  pretty fun house mirror spin on an  original episode we would never do just  like a karaoke version of an episode but  every now and then we'll do our take on  the original episode we have one in  season one but for the most part its  original stories that have allusions to  the original series that tackle some of  the same social issues of the original  series but are completely new and  different and unique stories as a  society love and easter-egg I noticed a  billion in the show can you talk about  some of the nods you paid to the  original series in this well I don't  ruin anything for fans I would let the  discover themselves trailer I will say  we see the gremlin we see the mystic  sphere yes yes oh good you know you've  definitely been studying doesn't  homework yeah um yeah we wanted this to  be a show that obviously kids or  teenagers or I mean folks really like  sort of in their twenties and thirties  who didn't grow up watching even the  reruns could watch and not necessarily  have to know anything about the original  series but the hope is that it can also  speak to the people that loved the  original series and it can get a new  generation watching the original series  for the first time and discovering what  we all know which is that it's one of  the greatest TV shows in history and so  we have lots of illusions lots of little  references whether they be props lines  sometimes like deep background things in  the production design the art design of  the show and then there's a lot of  issues that we tackle that we feel like  you know we tackle in this slightly  different way but rod was doing in his  own way too before I let you go I gotta  say we have to fight a little bit  because I watched the Dark Phoenix  trailer and I'm like he's really gonna  kill off my girl mystique in the freakin  trailer but that's also made me think  what else is gonna happen at this movie  if that could be in the trailer so I  mean are we gonna lose not everybody's  gonna die I can promise you that that's  not a spoiler but you know that the the  